SUMMARY:FreeOnFriday?  Noodle Doozy (27R) - NEW ROUTE!
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nRIDE LEADER: Jan Zerfoss\
 , average pace 12-13 mph.\nCue and Ride with GPS link: [Noodle Doozy](http
 s://ridewithgps.com/routes/55843953)\n**Be Safe\, Have Fun\, and Ride Toge
 ther**\n\nThis is a casual ride and the ride leader will ride at the adver
 tised pace. Some riders may ride faster than the leader so we'll likely br
 eak into one or more smaller groups. We will stop to regroup periodically.
  Please stay with other riders in your pace group so everyone has someone 
 to ride with and nobody is riding solo. Usually no designated sweep but no
 body will get dropped.\n\nThe start location is Grounded Coffeehouse at th
 e Ironspire Complex. Grounded has bathrooms we may use.\n\nPost-ride coffe
 e/refreshments - [Grounded Coffeehouse](https://www.facebook.com/p/Grounde
 d-Coffeehouse-61579210356629/) There is indoor and outdoor seating.\n\nLea
 rn about Noodle Doozy. AKA Noodle Doosie/Doozey. [Learn more about Noodle 
 Doozy](https://lancasteronline.com/opinion/noodle-doosie-cant-get-there-fr
 om-here/article_61257117-76a3-5fc3-8b47-58626624ddad.html)\n\nHelmets are 
 mandatory. No earbuds. Please bring water and a basic repair kit (spare tu
 be\, tire levers\, pump/CO2 inflator).\n\nTo eliminate passing around a pe
 n and paper waiver\, we require LBC Club membership and Meetup RSVP below 
 to join this ride. Being on\nMeetup does not mean you are a club member. J
 oin here [Member Signup](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?pa
 ge_id=60&club_id=257148)\n\nYour RSVP is your agreement to abide by the cl
 ub's Code of Conduct: [Code of Conduct](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/
 content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=323984)\n\nGuidance if an
  incident occurs: [Incident Actions](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/content
 .aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=326137)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-bicycle-club/events/3154331
